---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { launch, launchLabel, site, sourceUrl } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Roadmap" description="What shipped in NMSh v0.20.0, the validation still open and future proposals, with source links and no invented shipping dates.">
  <div class="container"><header class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Direction / Built in the open</span><h1>What’s taking shape.</h1><p class="lead">A clear view of the product, the work being finished and the ideas that still need testing.</p></header>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Shipped in v0.20.0.</h2><p>The {launchLabel} release brings the existing frontend together with the terminal workflow, a reviewed first run, background tasks and expanded context. <a href="/releases/">Release notes and history →</a></p></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Released</span><div><h3>Commands, output and continuity</h3><p>A persistent composer and shell, live sessions, serial queue, execution timeline, output selection, Copy Actions, reviewed reports and comparisons.</p><a class="text-link spaced" href="/docs/execution/">Execution workflows <span>→</span></a></div></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Released</span><div><h3>Work alongside the shell</h3><p>Session-owned background tasks, managed Claude Code beta, worktree tools, read-only GitHub inspection and a larger native module catalog. The experimental workspace sidebar remains Off by default.</p><a class="text-link spaced" href="/docs/integrations/">Tools and workspaces <span>→</span></a></div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Still being validated.</h2><p>Shipping a feature and proving it on every host are separate steps. Automated tests are not physical acceptance.</p></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Released</span><div><h3>First-run setup and Tools</h3><p>The Reactive Horizon starting point, guided Setup and the shared Tools flow shipped in v0.20.0 and were physically accepted on macOS.</p><a class="text-link spaced" href="/docs/setup/">Setup and first run <span>→</span></a></div></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Validation</span><div><h3>Real hosts beyond macOS</h3><p>Item-by-item checklist passes in Ghostty and Terminal.app, and any physical Linux, Omarchy or WSL 2 pass, are still open. Linux remains beta on automated CI.</p><a class="text-link spaced" href="/docs/reference/physical-qa/">Physical QA record <span>→</span></a></div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Future proposals.</h2><p>Directions worth investigating, not scheduled commitments. Scope, feasibility, security and design approval can change what eventually ships.</p></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Planned · Future</span><div><h3>Learn the command line by doing</h3><p>Guided Bash/zsh lessons, practice files, helpful feedback and resumable progress. Strong real-shell isolation must be verified, or execution must be explicitly simulated or disabled.</p><a class="text-link spaced" href="/learn/">Explore future Learn Mode <span>→</span></a></div></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Research / proposal</span><div><h3>Broader integrations, without blurred authority</h3><p>Additional managed-agent adapters, workflow tool integrations and stronger isolation for executable mods require independent capability and security evidence.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href={`${site.repo}/issues/339`}>Agent adapters · #339 <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={`${site.repo}/issues/341`}>Executable-mod isolation · #341 <span>↗</span></a></div></div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><p class="muted measure">Reviewed {launch.verifiedAt}. See the <a href={sourceUrl('ROADMAP.md')}>source roadmap</a> and <a href={`${site.repo}/issues`}>public issues</a> for the full context. An open issue is not automatically a product commitment.</p></section>
  </div>
</Base>
